claimed: okay-script-tls -- operator ask 2026-09-07: HTTPS for a Site. Three additive steps on the ONE transport seam specs/tls.md names: (1) okay-tls exposes Tls.serverContext(certFile, key, secrets): Either[String, SSLContext] -- serverSocket's own context, named, so a server that is not a ServerSocket can terminate TLS too; (2) okay-jetty's serve gains ssl: Option[SSLContext] = None beside ws/push (SslContextFactory.Server with setSslContext + SslConnectionFactory over the HttpConnectionFactory; no new dependency -- SSLContext is the JDK); (3) Site.serve(port, ssl) and okay.script.Serve reading OKAY_TLS_CERT + OKAY_TLS_KEY (a Secret ref, file:/ or env:), which prints an https:// URL. Live test: openssl self-signed cert, a real HTTPS GET of a page. Touches okay-tls/Tls.scala, okay-jetty/Jetty.scala (flagged: shared module, additive default), build.sbt (okayScript gains okayTls), Site.scala, Serve.scala, specs/okay-script.md + specs/tls.md.
